===== path p list
List available sources (branches, projects, sessions)

Usage: path p list [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  git       List git branches in a repository
  github    List GitHub pull requests
  claude    List Claude projects or sessions
  gemini    List Gemini CLI projects or sessions
  codex     List Codex CLI sessions (global, newest first)
  copilot   List GitHub Copilot CLI sessions (global, newest first; preview)
  opencode  List opencode sessions (global, newest first)
  cursor    List Cursor (IDE) composers (global, newest first). Reads `<user-data>/User/globalStorage/state.vscdb`
  pi        List Pi (pi.dev) projects or sessions
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (default: pretty when stdout is a TTY, tsv when piped)

          Possible values:
          - pretty: Human-readable, with section headers and aligned columns
          - json:   One JSON object per call
          - tsv:    One session per line, tab-delimited. See README for column layout

      --json
          Output as JSON (deprecated alias for --format json)

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path p list claude
List Claude projects or sessions

Usage: path p list claude [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -p, --project <PROJECT>
          Project path — if omitted, lists all projects (pretty) or all sessions across all projects (tsv/json)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (default: pretty when stdout is a TTY, tsv when piped)

          Possible values:
          - pretty: Human-readable, with section headers and aligned columns
          - json:   One JSON object per call
          - tsv:    One session per line, tab-delimited. See README for column layout

